Two Pointers

Idea
Use two indices to traverse a structure.
Instead of nested loops, pointers move through the array in a controlled way.

Two main versions: Opposite directions && same direction.

Opposite directions
left -> start
right -> end
Used when array is sorted.
Example:
while left < right
    sums = nums[left] + nums[right]
    if sum < target
        left ++
    if sum > target
        right--
    else
        found solution

Same direction
Two pointers move forward together.
Often used in sliding window problems.

Why it helps
Reduces time complexity.
Nested loop, O(n^2) to Two Pointer, O(n)
